STATUS: Create a matched set of three low, wide chapter-map-preview thumbnails
for the campaign selector. These are miniature previews of the complete map
compositions, not symbolic chapter icons. All three must fit side by side on
the existing shallow parchment backplate.

## Reference images

- Attach the user-provided campaign-screen reference screenshot. Use only its
  upper-right chapter selector to match the thumbnails' compact, horizontal
  proportions and small scenic-preview treatment. Do not recreate the screen.
- Attach
  `assets_src/campaign/chapter-maps/campaign_chapter_01_green_frontier_map.png`
  as the primary terrain reference for Chapter 1.
- Attach
  `assets_src/campaign/chapter-maps/campaign_chapter_02_broken_valley_map.png`
  as the primary terrain reference for Chapter 2. Do not substitute the
  existing square crystal emblem; it is not a map preview.
- Attach
  `assets_src/campaign/chapter-maps/campaign_chapter_03_ashen_march_map.png`
  as the primary terrain reference for Chapter 3.
- Attach `assets_src/campaign/ui/campaign_chapter_selector_parchment.png`
  only to understand the shared panel's shallow horizontal proportions. Do not
  bake the parchment into any thumbnail.
- Create a readable miniature preview of each chapter's environment rather
  than inventing a detached emblem.

## Output

- Generate exactly one PNG sprite sheet:
  `campaign_chapter_thumbnails_sheet.png`.
- Save it under `assets_src/campaign/chapter-thumbnails/`.
- Canvas: exactly 1536 x 288 pixels, horizontal, opaque RGB or RGBA with a
  fully opaque alpha channel.
- Arrange exactly three equal 512 x 288 pixel cells side by side:
  1. Chapter 1 thumbnail, using the Green Frontier map.
  2. Chapter 2 thumbnail, using the Broken Valley map.
  3. Chapter 3 thumbnail, using the Ashen March map.
- Each cell is a 16:9 landscape thumbnail. Fill the cell edge to edge with
  artwork; do not leave transparent padding or add a gutter between cells.
- These are three carousel assets, not three simultaneously visible tiles. The
  312 x 104 dp parchment viewport shows two framed cards at once. Each card
  uses a 144 x 74 dp layout slot and is rendered at 80% scale (about
  115 x 59 dp).
- Each frame's clear image window is approximately 126 x 51 dp (about 2.47:1).
  The 80% presentation scale makes the visible window about 101 x 41 dp.
  Android center-crops the 16:9 thumbnail into this shallow panoramic window;
  compose each preview so its strongest terrain and route/site pattern remains
  recognizable in a central horizontal band.
- Keep all previews at the same scale, camera distance, detail density, and
  painterly finish so they read as a coordinated set.

## Thumbnail direction

- Show a compact, painterly miniature map preview of each chapter. Preserve
  the reference map's geography, route flow, and empty site clearings; do not
  invent a new route or move sites. Compose the 16:9 source so its central
  horizontal crop remains representative when shown in the 101 x 41 dp
  rendered window.
  Simplify small textures while retaining broad, legible terrain shapes and
  the distinctive chapter palette.
- **Chapter 1 — The Green Frontier:** show the lush green frontier from
  the supplied Chapter 1 map, using its characteristic vegetation, hills,
  waterways, and warm natural palette.
- **Chapter 2 — The Broken Valley:** match the fractured valley in the
  supplied Chapter 2 map, using its cold palette and broken terrain.
- **Chapter 3 — The Ashen March:** match the ashen basin, scorched ridges, and
  restrained ember glow in the supplied Chapter 3 map.
- Keep the camera angle and degree of detail consistent with the reference
  maps. Do not shift, add, remove, or rearrange the ten site clearings or their
  connecting route.
- Let each image fill its wide rectangle. Keep focal terrain and important
  route and site details legible after reduction; avoid placing critical detail
  at the outermost few pixels where the UI may overlay status badges.
- Use clear, readable silhouettes and restrained details. Avoid tiny
  structures, particles, or textures that collapse into noise when reduced.
- Keep all thumbnails equally bright and complete. Do not dim locked or
  completed chapters; selection, completion, and lock states are live UI.

## Separation from the parchment and live UI

- Generate only the three landscape thumbnails. The shared parchment and
  frame are separate UI assets and must not be baked into any cell.
- Do not add an individual card, frame, border, tab shape, ribbon, or rounded
  tile around any thumbnail. The images are placed directly on the shared
  parchment.
- Do not include chapter numbers, names, title text, letters, runes that
  resemble writing, locks, checkmarks, progress indicators, or selection
  treatments.
- Do not reproduce the whole campaign screenshot, outer map frame, Back
  control, Start Level button, HUD, or unrelated screen elements.
- Do not add captions, decorative badges, detached glow, shadows, or
  transparent margins.
- Keep any terrain or landmark detail faithful to the matching map. Do not add
  unrelated characters, enemies, weapons, or gameplay scenes.

## Review and extraction

- Confirm the output is exactly 1536 x 288 pixels and contains exactly three
  edge-to-edge 512 x 288 landscape previews in Chapter 1 / Chapter 2 / Chapter
  3 order.
- Confirm each cell reads as a miniature of its complete campaign map, not as a
  symbol, crest, or square app icon.
- Confirm all three thumbnails share the same camera scale and visual
  treatment, while their landscapes and palettes remain clearly distinct.
- Confirm no individual card frame, text, chapter number, lock, checkmark, or
  parchment is baked into the artwork.
- Confirm each map remains recognizable after a center crop to the shallow
  126 x 51 dp frame window. Confirm the UI can show two framed cards at a time
  on the 312 x 104 dp parchment panel, with separate captions and status
  badges.
- After approval, split the actual sprite sheet into three 512 x 288 RGBA
  source assets without changing the composition or trimming any thumbnail.
  Name them `campaign_chapter_01_thumbnail.png`,
  `campaign_chapter_02_thumbnail.png`, and
  `campaign_chapter_03_thumbnail.png` in that order.
- Do not import a newly generated replacement set into Android until all
  previews have been reviewed and approved; preserve the installed thumbnail
  set until then.

## Negative prompt

symbolic icon, square icon, emblem, crest, medallion, isolated leaf, isolated
crystal, isolated object, portrait composition, tall composition, full campaign
screen, UI screenshot, button, card, individual tile, card frame, border,
parchment background, ribbon, chapter number, chapter name, title, text,
letters, writing, runes, lock, checkmark, progress bar, selection glow,
darkened locked state, badge, HUD, Back control, Start Level control,
single-landscape crop, modified route, added or missing site clearing, changed
map geography, mismatched camera scale, inconsistent art style, tiny
unreadable detail, noise, detached shadow, detached glow, particles, watermark,
signature
